<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vesdre</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vesdre is a river of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, about 70 km long, rising in the High Fens near the German border and joining the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ourthe">Ourthe</a> near Liège. It flows past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eupen">Eupen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limbourg">Limbourg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verviers">Verviers</a>, and its soft water powered the region's wool-cloth industry. In July 2021 it caused devastating floods along its valley.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vesdre.jpg" alt="Vesdre" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Pol GRANDMONT · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Limbourg_JPG03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
